{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the officers shall add.</b> Why is ויספו said here? They add this to the words of the priest — for the priest speaks and proclaims from שמע ישראל until להושיע אתכם, and מי האיש and a second and a third — the priest speaks and the officer proclaims, and this one speaks and this officer proclaims (Sotah 43)." "<b>Who is fearful and faint-hearted.</b> Rabbi Akiva says, as it sounds — that he cannot stand in the battle lines and see a drawn sword. Rabbi Yosei the Galilean says: one who fears the transgressions in his hand. Therefore the Torah gave him cause to return on account of house, vineyard, and wife, to cover over those returning because of transgressions in their hands, so that they not be recognized as bearers of transgression. And whoever sees him returning says: perhaps he built a house, or planted a vineyard, or betrothed a wife (Sotah 44)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:48.216061463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}